{"t": 1794109213.4158573, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": ":rotating_light: *AG-7731 \u2014 PaymentGatewayErrors checkout* (critical)\n\n*What's wrong:* checkout is sending charge amounts to the payment gateway as decimal euros (e.g. `{\"amount\": 12.34, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`). The gateway switched to API version 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\") at 07:41 UTC and now rejects any non-integer `amount` with `400 invalid_amount: amount must be an integer in minor units (cents)`. This is driving the 38% gateway 4xx rate since 07:41 UTC.\n\n*Fix:* `checkout/gateway.py` \u2014 `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (`Decimal(str(amount_eur)) * 100`, ROUND_HALF_UP) before building the payload. E.g. 12.34 -> `{\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`. Currency field unchanged; verified locally across normal and edge-case amounts.\n\n*Status:* code fixed in the working tree, not yet deployed. Next step is to roll out checkout; the 4xx rate should drop to ~0 and the alert should clear once the new build is serving. No data loss \u2014 the gateway rejected the requests, so no duplicate charges.\n\nPing me if you need the diff or the deploy."}, "ok": true}
